### part 2
disc P = -209869400103889499760776960 {2: 8, 5: 1, 31: 1, 367: 2, 104053: 1, 614321: 2, -1: 1}

== Gal(P) = S8 certificate (Dedekind: unramified Frobenius cycle type = factorisation type mod p)
smallest unramified primes with these factorisation types: {'(7,1)': 7, '(2,1^6)': 8017, '(8)': 29, '(5,3)': 23}
Proof: P irreducible => G transitive; Frobenius at p = 7 is a 7-cycle => G 2-transitive => primitive; Frobenius at p = 8017 is a transposition; a primitive group containing a transposition is S_n (Jordan). So G = S8.

== Dedekind criterion: is Z[T] p-maximal?
   p =       2: v_p(disc P) = 8, factorisation mod p = [(2, 4)], Z[T] p-maximal: True
   p =       5: v_p(disc P) = 1, factorisation mod p = [(1, 1), (1, 2), (5, 1)], Z[T] p-maximal: True
   p =      31: v_p(disc P) = 1, factorisation mod p = [(1, 1), (1, 2), (5, 1)], Z[T] p-maximal: True
   p =     367: v_p(disc P) = 2, factorisation mod p = [(1, 2), (3, 1), (3, 1)], Z[T] p-maximal: False
   p =  104053: v_p(disc P) = 1, factorisation mod p = [(1, 2), (6, 1)], Z[T] p-maximal: True
   p =  614321: v_p(disc P) = 2, factorisation mod p = [(1, 1), (1, 1), (1, 2), (2, 1), (2, 1)], Z[T] p-maximal: False

   Conclusion for d_K (disc P = index^2 * d_K):
   p-maximal at p  =>  v_p(d_K) = v_p(disc P); not p-maximal with v_p(disc P) = 2  =>  v_p(d_K) = 0 (index divisible by p).

